# Metro's file crawler cannot cope with pnpm's default hardlinked node_modules
# on Windows: expo-router ships many byte-identical trivial stub files (all the
# `types.js` re-export shims), pnpm hardlinks them to a single inode in its
# content-addressable store, and Metro's crawler then registers only one of
# them — every other path "does not exist". The result is a nondeterministic
# "Unable to resolve module ./types" from a different expo-router internal file
# on every cold bundle.
#
# Verified with a minimal reproducer (a bare create-expo-app + expo-router,
# no monorepo, no custom metro config): npm bundles fine, pnpm fails, and
# pnpm with this setting bundles fine. node-linker=hoisted does NOT help,
# because it still hardlinks.
#
# Trade-off: installs copy instead of hardlink, so node_modules uses more disk
# and installs are somewhat slower. That is the cost of a working bundler.
package-import-method=copy
